            id: "u11-h-title-premature", kind: "hypo", cat: "III.C", callType: "remedy", rule: "u11-r-marketable", issue: "marketability tested at closing", grid: true,
            stem: "A seller contracted to sell a house for $400,000, to be conveyed free of encumbrances, with closing in six weeks. Three weeks before closing, the buyer's title search showed an unpaid $90,000 mortgage on the house. The buyer at once notified the seller that the contract was cancelled and demanded return of the $20,000 deposit. The seller replied that the mortgage would be paid from the sale proceeds at closing and that she would deliver a recorded satisfaction. The buyer did not respond and did not appear at closing.",
