            stem: "A landowner was 10 years old when a neighbor began openly occupying the landowner's vacant lot without permission. The jurisdiction's statute provides that an action to recover land must be brought within 15 years after it accrues, but if the owner is a minor when the cause of action accrues, within 15 years after the minority ends (age 18). The neighbor occupied the lot continuously for 20 years, until the landowner was 30, and then the landowner sued for possession.",
